                <pb facs="0288" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg216"/>

                <head>Municipal Council of Emerald Hill</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Borough Council Chamber</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Emerald Hill</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-08-04">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">August</hi> 4, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, by desire of the council
                    of the borough of Emerald Hill, to forward herewith a copy of a resolution
                    unanimously passed by the council at the last meeting, being an expression of
                    the council’s sympathy with the widow of the late and lamented President of the
                    United States of America in her sore bereavement; and also the council’s deep
                    abhorrence of the dastardly act which has removed from the sphere of his
                    usefulness one of the greatest men of modern times, and one who no doubt, had he
                    lived, would have restored America to her original tranquillity and prosperity.
                    I am further desired to request the favor of your kindly forwarding the enclosed
                    to Mrs. Lincoln by the first opportunity.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN WHITEMAN, J. P., </signed>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mayor</hi>. </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Blanchard</hi>, Esq., <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Consul of the United States of America</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
